<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1595–<a href="/years/1657">1657</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bohdan Khmelnytsky was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> leader who led a major uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> from 1648. The revolt caused catastrophic losses and led to an alliance with Muscovy. His forces were among the invaders during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-deluge">Deluge</a> of 1655–1660, which devastated the Commonwealth and accelerated its decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky.jpg" alt="Bohdan Khmelnytsky" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bohdan_Khmelnytsky.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
